---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { articles } from '../../articles.js';

const meta = articles.find((article) => article.slug === 'ai');
---

<Base
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  ogType="article">
  <section class="mt-6 max-w-prose md:mt-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
      "We have the latest model, why do we need developers?"
    </h1>
    <h2 class="lede mt-3 text-lg font-bold">
      What are you saying? A good AI collaborator is someone who knows their domain first &amp; delegates to AI second?
      Nah! Go sell potatoes!
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-right font-mono text-sm opacity-60">
      <time datetime="2026-09-11">11/09/2026</time>
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
      <p>There's a wage reduction fantasy every generation.</p>
      <p>AI &gt; No/low code &gt; RAD tools &amp; SAP &gt; MS Access &amp; SharePoint ...etc.</p>
      <p>You need to learn to bite your tongue &amp; let the higher ups hit the wall with a full erecti*n.</p>
      <p>YES! Practically every white collar job is solved, not just coding. But for who though?</p>
      <p>Vibe coding on localhost:8080 is not the same thing as a multi team/service system in prod.</p>
      <p>
        Unless you have unlimited access or a FAANG budget, anyone on a limited plan has already run into the
        shortcomings. Past a certain usage, which you hit pretty fast in any prod codebase, quality drops &amp; shadow
        rerouting kicks in: fast &amp; cheap band aids, with little ability to step back or plan for consequences.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can always try to mitigate through orchestration, skills &amp; context management. But the only real fix is
        money: continuous billing &amp; burning more tokens.
      </p>
      <p>
        This will stay a hard constraint as long as major providers are running at a loss, which they will be for a
        while, because of energy.
      </p>
      <p>
        The race for infinite growth on a finite planet leads nowhere but{' '}
        <a
          class="link"
          href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enshittification"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">
          enshittification
        </a>
        . Once Big Tech is done scorching earth, 💩 floodgates will open, prices will reach orbit &amp; decision makers
        will go on a cruise.
      </p>
      <figure class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-center">
        <img
          class="rounded-box border-base-300 border"
          alt="McDonald's CEO"
          decoding="async"
          height="300"
          loading="lazy"
          src="/ceo.png"
          width="300"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-sm opacity-70">
          <a
            class="link"
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W6QFxgS8fSA"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank">
            McDonald's CEO enjoying his PRODUK
          </a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
